+### 2026-08-14 Runtime-Cache Accepted-Descriptor Repair
+
+The shared frame-resolution refactor separates artifact rehydration, pending
+runtime-bake reservation, and graph-key selection. Its accepted-descriptor
+fast path must use the same producer-aware currentness rule as payload
+hydration: CPU asset-derived descriptors use `is_current_for`, while GPU
+runtime-cache descriptors use `is_current_runtime_cache_for`. Treating every
+accepted descriptor as CPU-only would make a valid GPU result fall through to
+`RuntimeBakeUnavailable` after the four-entry memo is evicted, despite the
+already-hydrated environment retaining its complete immutable payload.
+
+- Implemented in the isolated rebased patch
+  `shader06-m8-runtime-cache-accepted-descriptor-rebased-20260814.patch`:
+  producer-aware accepted-descriptor validation preserves a current GPU
+  runtime-cache result without a memo or a cache-store lookup and keeps the
+  runtime bake graph out of the compile options.
+- The focused regression seeds a GPU-provenance runtime cache, hydrates it,
+  replaces the memo with an empty cache and the asset manager with its default
+  no-store state, then requires `Hydrated` with no bake request. The prior
+  CPU-only predicate returns `RuntimeBakeUnavailable` at that point.
+- Second independent review reported `Critical 0 / Important 0 / Minor 0`.
+  The patch applies cleanly over the shared resolver refactor. Managed Windows
+  Rust/WGPU validation remains pending; this entry does not claim acceptance.
